1795198399707706	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-12w	{"field":"description","value":"Per-destination caps do not show the address space covered by a whole pass. In check and status show the union of the declared address intervals, separately for IPv4 and IPv6, ignoring duplicate service rules and counting explicit whole-network approvals. Describe it as declared address space, which can include IPv4 edges. Keep very large values exact for JSON clients.\n\nAccept with disjoint, nested and repeated networks, single hosts, both families and the maximum destination count. Proptest small IPv4 unions against enumeration and confirm invariance under order and duplication. Show exact large IPv6 results without enumerating hosts. Use the documented consumer caps in the original rationale (one IPv4 /8 and one IPv6 /64) as comparison points. Record whether Hallpass warns or rejects at the selected totals, including the behavior of previously valid passes, before making any validation change. Update docs/PASS-FORMAT.md and docs/spec.md."}	blake3:CKQUQFenrq5ASSxiRjnh3Q0RINqCj89sEOgtMy42zPw
