1795198400480331	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-2uf	{"field":"description","value":"A counted unit can require further read-only target checks. spend accepts the digest confirmed by the operator, while the documented follow-up permits invocation reloads the current pass without a digest precondition. Give callers a single way to keep a whole unit on the approved revision.\n\nDelivery\nAdd permits --digest and a path-based Rust operation accepting an optional expected Digest, explicit StateDir, target, name, instant and duration. Route the CLI through it. Load once per call, apply the existing ledger/witness checks, compare the expected digest with that LoadedPass, then decide against the very same Pass. Preserve pure in-memory methods.\n\nAcceptance\n- With a matching pin, existing named/unnamed decisions, warnings and exit codes are preserved. A stale valid pin gives pass-changed and exit 2 on an otherwise valid state, even for a comment edit. An invalid digest is a usage error.\n- A corrupt ledger remains an error. Apply the same witness policy as unpinned permits (bn-2rf owns that policy).\n- A CLI integration example spends against revision A, edits the pass while retaining its ID, and refuses the secondary check pinned to A. A call without a pin follows current behavior. Neither check appends a ledger entry.\n- Cover the same cases in the Rust path and update docs/INTEGRATING.md. No second spend is needed for a follow-up address.\n\nMatch the effective read-only witness contract, including any decision recorded in bn-2rf by the time this ships. The pin adds a digest precondition without deciding that policy. Pass an injected clock and StateDir in Rust tests, preserve existing exit precedence, and document --digest in docs/spec.md."}	blake3:-PSxJejqUJXY3ZWYxhxssBpxv5H1ZVCXJVwR6kkaI7o
