1795198401190724	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-d6g	{"field":"description","value":"The worked example in tests/integrating.rs checks the JSON Hallpass produces. It cannot tell an integrating team whether its own subprocess wrapper accidentally treats help output, malformed JSON or a contradictory exit code as permission. Give teams fixtures that exercise their decoder in their own CI.\n\nDelivery\nPublish a small language-neutral, versioned corpus of synthetic process outcomes (stdout, exit code or spawn failure, and expected client action) plus a minimal reference adapter in the integrating docs. Include one successful counted decision and one refusal captured from the real CLI. Use synthetic fixtures for transport or process failures which a healthy binary cannot emit. Drive a callback spy in the example so each case has an observable result without network I/O.\n\nAcceptance\n- Only the valid production-mode spend response advances the example callback. Explicitly cover exit 0 with help, nonzero with allowed JSON, refused/error, a permits response in place of spend, test_clock true, missing/truncated output and launch failure.\n- Additional unknown JSON fields remain compatible. A valid allowed response with warnings advances once and surfaces the warnings to the caller.\n- A test in the style of tests/integrating.rs checks the genuine cases against the binary and runs the reference decoder over all fixtures. Document how a second tool runs its own decoder against the same corpus without Rust or a live target.\n- Scope is the client decision boundary. Existing end-to-end tests keep ownership of the pass engine itself.\n\nUse production-mode true/false clock semantics in the genuine cases. tests/integrating.rs sets a fixed test clock, so generate a pass spanning the real test instant and unset the override for the genuine production allowance. Check the result belongs to the requested spend and includes its recorded sequence. Include a would-allow preview as a synthetic no-send case. Include the committed debit / witness failure contract from bn-37i as a no-send, reconcile-before-retry case. Keep the documented corpus readable by a non-Rust client's own test runner."}	blake3:FC6PzFPqaEonS0dWU362mcjTEFeRLbHl31R-u-xhyFA
